     120→## 7. Pass/Fail Criteria
     121→
     122→### All tests PASS when:
     123→1. `go build ./...` completes without errors
     124→2. `go vet ./...` completes without warnings
     125→3. `go test -timeout 5m -race ./...` all pass (12/12 tests)
     126→4. E2E scripts exist and are executable
     127→5. `screenshots/` directory exists with `.gitkeep`
     128→6. `.cast` file exists and is non-empty
     129→7. `.cast` file starts with `{` (valid asciinema JSON header)
     130→
     131→### Any test FAIL when:
     132→1. Build fails
     133→2. Vet reports issues
     134→3. Any test fails
     135→4. Race detector finds data races
     136→5. `.cast` file is empty or not in asciinema format
     137→
     138→## 8. Test Execution Summary
     139→
     140→- **Total Unit Tests**: 12
     141→- **Build Checks**: 2 (build, vet)
     142→- **Race Detection**: 1
     143→- **E2E Scripts**: 2 (e2e-screenshot.sh, asciinema.sh)
     144→
     145→All tests must PASS for this feature to be considered complete.
     146→
     147→## 9. Event-Driven Architecture Validation
     148→
     149→### Input Handling
     150→- Uses `termbox.PollEvent()` for blocking event-driven input
     151→- No background goroutine for input handling
     152→- Main loop handles all events synchronously
     153→
     154→### Game Restart Flow
     155→1. Game over detected in `Update()`
     156→2. `setGameOver(true)` called
     157→3. Main loop enters restart-wait loop (lines 186-197)
     158→4. User presses R → `reset()` called → game restarts
     159→5. User presses Esc/Ctrl+C → function returns, game exits
     160→
     161→This flow has no goroutine lifecycle issues because no input goroutine exists.
     162→
     163→## 10. Known Limitations
     164→
     165→### termbox-go in PTY
     166→- termbox-go may not initialize properly in all PTY environments
     167→- If termbox.Init() fails, the game will panic with "panic: error attempting to initialize terminal"
     168→- This is a known limitation and may cause E2E tests to fail in some environments
     169→
     170→### asciinema Python Bug
     171→- asciinema Python version 2.4.0 has a bug where it crashes with "ValueError: list.remove(x): x not in list" when terminated by timeout
     172→- The .cast file is still written correctly before the crash
     173→- stderr is suppressed in the script to avoid ugly traceback output
     174→
  
